### Describe the bug and how to replicate it

Install a plugin using ProtocolLib that modifies Set_Slot & Window_Items packets in any way.
In this example I set the Material of all items to TNT

This will cause repeated window_items/set_slot packets to be sent per item modified * however many players are on the server.
Showcase: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q2T-hZ7NK50

```
public class PacketDebugger extends PacketAdapter implements Listener {

    public PacketDebugger(@NotNull PacketAdapter.AdapterParameteters params) {
        super(params);
    }

    @Override
    public void onPacketSending(PacketEvent event) {
        Player player = event.getPlayer();
        if (player.getGameMode() == GameMode.CREATIVE) return;

        PacketContainer packet = event.getPacket();
        ItemStack item = packet.getItemModifier().read(0);
        if (item != null && !item.getType().isAir()) {
            item.setType(Material.TNT);
        }

        if (event.getPacketType() == PacketType.Play.Server.WINDOW_ITEMS) {
            player.sendMessage("WINDOW_ITEMS");
            List<ItemStack> items = packet.getItemListModifier().read(0);
            for (ItemStack itemStack : items) {
                if (itemStack != null && !itemStack.getType().isAir()) {
                    itemStack.setType(Material.TNT);
                }
            }
        } else {
            player.sendMessage("SET_SLOT");
        }
    }
}

