    player.packetStateData.lastRiptide = currentTime;
}

// later in code
// line 569 in MovementCheckRunner
if (player.packetStateData.tryingToRiptide != clientClaimsRiptide) {
    player.getSetbackTeleportUtil().executeForceResync(); // Could technically be lag due to packet timings.
}
```

Not sure why the check that checks last riptide time and water passes and causes setback (maybe the code is ran twice for some reason?), but commenting out the check on line 569 gets rid of the setback (though not the simulation/groundspoof falses).

